# Line endings are normalised to LF, both in the repository and in the working
# tree, whatever core.autocrlf a given clone happens to have set.
#
# Without the explicit `eol=lf`, a clone with autocrlf=true (the Git for
# Windows default, and what a WSL checkout often inherits) writes CRLF to disk.
# Prettier's endOfLine default is lf, so `npm run format:check` then fails on
# every file in the tree -- including files nobody has touched -- while CI,
# which checks out on Linux, passes. That divergence is the bug this prevents.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Extracted assets. Never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
